    "problem_statement": "GetRowMatch returns incorrect row numbers after indentation fix\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `GetRowMatch` method in `IndexTable` is returning incorrect row numbers. When matching attributes against index rows, the method should return the actual row number from the index, but it's currently returning modified values.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport textfsm.clitable as clitable\n\n# Create a simple index table\nindex_data = \"\"\"Template, Hostname, Platform, Command\ntemplate1, .*, cisco_ios, show version\ntemplate2, .*, cisco_ios, show interfaces\ntemplate3, .*, juniper, show version\"\"\"\n\n# Create CliTable and test GetRowMatch\ncli_table = clitable.CliTable('index', 'templates')\ncli_table.index.ParseIndex(index_data)\n\n# Test matching attributes\nattributes = {'Hostname': 'router1', 'Platform': 'cisco_ios', 'Command': 'show version'}\nrow_match = cli_table.index.GetRowMatch(attributes)\n\nprint(f\"Expected row: 1, Got row: {row_match}\")\n```\n\nThe method is expected to return the correct row number that matches the attributes, but instead returns unexpected values. This affects template selection and parsing functionality throughout the CliTable system."
